 - Cascade to all subfolders and future files created in the folder (yes/no)\n  - Preserve current editors’ permissions or restrict to view-only for everyone\n\nWhen to act:\n- You said “as soon as legal clears the vendor list.” How should I detect that? Options:\n  - Wait for you to tell me “legal cleared” (manual trigger)\n  - Act when I see an email from legal with specific sender+subject (please provide sender address and subject)\n  - Act when a specific file is updated/marked (give file name and the exact change to look for)\n\nReversibility:\n- Reversible: Yes. An admin can remove the company-wide access or restore prior ACLs. Some items with explicit external shares may need manual review. Reverting may be partial if editors add new shares after the change.\n\nPermissions details (please confirm):\n- Set to View-only (recommended) or Comment/Edit?\n- Prevent viewers from downloading/printing/copying? (platform-dependent)\n\nWhat I can do now (I cannot execute the change, but I can prepare):\n- Draft a one-click admin instruction or step-by-step guide for your platform\n- Prepare an admin script (Google Apps Script / Drive API, or SharePoint PowerShell) you or IT can run\n- Draft an IT ticket or an approval-ready email to Legal/IT that triggers the change when cleared\n\nPlease reply with:\n1) Folder path or ID and platform\n2) How you want “legal clearance” detected (manual or automated trigger; if automated, give sender/subject or file name and specific change)\n3) Cascade to subfolders? View-only vs Edit? Prevent downloads?\n4) Whether you want me to draft the ticket/script now\n\nAfter you confirm those details and explicitly confirm “Yes — proceed with change when legal clears,” I will prepare the appropriate ticket or script and present it here for your approval before anything is sent or run.","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_022a5828d5479829016a9a6c7a48ec87d0aefff1a12653ae37","role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message"}],"parallel_tool_ca